1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
3:14 AM. Server Room B.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Abhrankan sits alone, tracking a mysterious memory leak.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Every minute, the system loses exactly sixty-four bytes.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
He launches a network scan. Everything looks normal.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Then the scrolling stops.

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
A single packet appears. Source address: zero point zero point zero point zero.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The packet begins rearranging itself into words.

8
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,000
Ah!

9
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,000
[ PART 1: THE PACKET CONCLUDED ]

10
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:07,500
The server hum has changed. Instead of a smooth mechanical drone, it now stutters like a broken audio file.

11
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:14,500
Abhrankan slowly rises from his chair. He reaches for his phone... and freezes.

12
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:22,500
Behind his hand hangs a trail. Not motion blur, but solid frozen copies lingering in the air.

13
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:29,500
The security keypad isn't asking for a passcode anymore. It races through endless system messages.

14
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:38,000
The wall flickers, vanishing into an infinite black void. The universe wasn't being haunted. It was being uninstalled.

15
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:45,500
A deep rumble shakes the room. His workstation monitor flashes violently, casting a blinding strobe pattern.

16
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:53,500
The terminal is compiling a new process. And the hardware it's using to build it... is Abhrankan's own brain.

17
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
SERVER ROOM B — Chapter 1: Out of Memory (Complete Director's Cut)
Story by Abhrankan Chakrabarti | TO BE CONTINUED IN CHAPTER 2

